+  - **Extend (R1, R2; §12A.17 T):** a scheduled lifetime grant (start in the future) rejects Extend. Revoking every non-revoked lifetime grant allows Extend again. Month-end clamping: a one-month extension from 31 January at 15:00 IST ends 28 February at 15:00 IST (29 February in a leap year). Every unsupported unit is rejected, for example day, week, six months, two years, or an empty value.
+  - **Overlap (R3; §12A.6; RPC-enforced):** same-kind overlap rejected for admin with admin and for lifetime with lifetime. Touching intervals allowed, for example one grant ends at 00:00 IST on a date and the next starts at that instant. An admin grant over a lifetime grant allowed. A revoked coverage does not block a new same-kind grant.
+  - **Counter and detail failures (C2, R7; §12A.17 G):** a synthetic failure of an actor counter write, a global counter write, or a required detail write each (a) raises, (b) rolls back every write in the transaction, (c) returns no committed `forbidden`, and (d) executes no protected operation. Separately, a cap omission writes no detail row, keeps the exact `denial_count` rising, leaves `detail_count` unchanged, and gives an omitted count of `denial_count − detail_count`.
+  - **Reason (R6; §12A.17 S):** Extend, Grant, Revoke and Replace each require a reason. A missing reason, or one that is empty after trimming, or one over 500 code points, is rejected with the validation code. The same normalised value appears in the coverage row and the audit row.
 
